.DS_Store
artifacts
# Scratch CMake configure/build trees and negative-control sources the native lanes drop at the
# repository root while proving a gate reds. Anchored so a package's own `build/` still answers to
# the ignore rules in its own tree.
/build/
# Android NDK simpleperf downloads device binaries here while symbolizing a profile.
binary_cache/
.playwright-mcp
# Godot's per-project import cache, regenerated by the opt-in engine load test export.
benchmark/godot-load-test/.godot/
hosting/.data/
# A sweep archive is half evidence and half build output, and only the second half leaves git
# (PRD-323 Phase 4). The tree held 5,292 tracked files, of which 2,963 were generated arm `.ts`
# game sources — crossed by every repo-wide grep an agent runs, the same hazard the root
# `AGENTS.md` names for `.worktrees/` at five times the file count.
#
# **The measurement artifacts stay tracked**, and this is not a preference: `sweep-ledger.spec.ts`
# fails with "live ledger requires committed proof.json", `sweep-delta.spec.ts` matches "the
# committed delta record" against archived measurements, and `capture.spec.ts` reads a real
# archived frame at `platformer-2026-08-06/proof-artifacts/0/after.png`. A first attempt ignored
# the whole tree; it passed locally, where the files are on disk, and failed three suites in CI,
# where they are not. `sweep.json`, `proof.json`, `proof-artifacts/`, `playtests/`, `captures/`,
# `screenshots/`, `brief.md` and `reference.png` are the record and are carried.
#
# What leaves is the regenerable arm source each run writes: `src/`, `starter-baseline/`,
# `framework-types/`, `public/` and the scaffold's root config files. Those hold all 2,963 `.ts`
# and none of the measurements. The whole archive stays on disk either way, and every sweep
# command still works — `sweep-archive.ts`, `sweep-capture.ts`, `sweep-judge.ts`, `sweep-pair.ts`
# and `make-sandbox.ts` all resolve this tree through the filesystem, never through git.
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/src/
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/starter-baseline/
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/framework-types/
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/public/
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/vite.config.ts
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/tailwind.config.ts
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/threenative.config.ts
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/package.json
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/tsconfig.json
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/index.html
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/pnpm-lock.yaml
# Third-party models a sweep was handed as source material. The FPS kit's first-person viewmodel
# records "user-provided; verify upstream pack terms before redistribution" and its enemy is
# CC-BY-4.0 carrying retargeted Mixamo clips, so neither is ours to redistribute from an MIT
# repository. The archive keeps them on disk; git does not carry them.
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/vendor/
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/assets/models/
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/assets/imported/
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/assets/generated/
# Builder session transcripts: the archived evidence a cold run happened, but ~8 MB of gzipped
# JSONL each carrying absolute paths from the machine that ran them. Commit one deliberately with
# `git add -f` if a result is disputed; do not carry every run's in history by default.
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/transcript.jsonl.gz
.linchpin/
.gauntlet/

# Shared editor settings are committed — they keep VS Code's watcher and TypeScript server out
# of the 6+ GB of build output under packages/runtime-native. Everything else VS Code drops in
# here is per-machine and is not.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json

# Other agents' lanes. Never searched, never read; see AGENTS.md.
.worktrees

# Secrets. Never committed, never copied into an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# written by installing @threenative/core (workspace link writes it at the repo root too)
.mcp.json
# ...except the template copies, which are shipped source. The pattern above is unanchored, so it
# swallowed the config of every template added after it: the file generated fine, `git status` said
# nothing, and the scaffold shipped without it. That surfaced as four scaffold suites failing on
#   Error: Scaffold produced no .mcp.json at '.../puzzle/.mcp.json'
# for templates whose config was present on the author's disk the whole time.
!packages/create-threenative/templates/*/.mcp.json
/.codex/

# generated from packages/engine-mcp/dist during the core package build
packages/assets/dist/blender-gpl/

# Sandbox mini-game captures, left at the root for inspection. Not part of the repo.
screenshot-*.png

# `pnpm pack` output. Several gates pack the workspace into `packages/*.tgz` to install a
# scaffold the way a stranger's machine would; three of them were committed by accident in #37.
*.tgz

# The site's Playwright output. The prerendered artifact under site/dist is already ignored.
site/test-results/

# Python bytecode caches. `packages/blender-mcp/gpl/recipes` is executed by Blender, which
# writes a `__pycache__` beside the recipes on every run; one .pyc was committed by accident.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
